 28	## Changes (all generic; nothing task-specific)
 29	
 30	| Area | Change |
 31	|---|---|
 32	| Dropped streams | A stream that ends without a finish reason counts as cut: complete blocks are kept and the rest is requested as a continuation. |
 33	| Retry after a drop | If a connection drops more than 60 s into an attempt, the retry uses lower effort (high → low → off), so it is shorter and more likely to finish. Early gateway errors keep the effort. |
 34	| Reasoning caps | Lowered to about 45k tokens for code (160k characters). A call still reasoning at the cap is aborted and retried at lower effort. |
 35	| Lost units | Every unit with no usable answer, or that failed verification, is retried once at low effort after all other units, before the repair phase. |
 36	| Test isolation | Local test runs start the host with a reset endpoint. Every local test starts from the freshly seeded data and freshly loaded backend modules. The endpoint does not exist unless the agent's own test runner sets `EVOGIT_TEST_RESET=1`, so the delivered app behaves exactly as before. |
 37	| Seed conflicts | The planning step also returns `seed_conflicts`: which content the seed holds when requirements disagree (the majority content), and which requirements' tests must first enter their own contents through the UI. These go into the implementation, repair and test prompts. |
 38	| Test defects | A test whose own code throws (`TypeError`, `ReferenceError`, `SyntaxError`) is not repaired against. Its file is rewritten once and re-run. |
 39	| Test runner | Clipboard permissions are granted (for paste scenarios). API responses of 400 and above are included in failure reports. |
 40	| Diagnostics | Log failure lines now carry the error's first line with its expected and received values. `MODEL_STATUS.json` stores the failing-test list after the units, at each checkpoint and at the end. The planned seed conflicts are logged. |
 41	| Time budget | `min(16 h, 840 s × leaves + 1 h)`: about 12 h for the larger task and 6.6 h for the smaller. |
